From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] Filer: the selected view is the state slate, not an ink block

Luma ADR-043. The view switcher's checked button filled with @luma_ink and
wrote @luma_content on it: correct as an inversion, but on the light window
it was a near-black square, the heaviest thing in the toolbar, for a control
that only says which view is showing. Ink is the one emphasis a view keeps;
a selected view is a state.

The checked button and its symbol now take libadwaita's --luma-state and
--luma-state-ink (libadwaita 0039), the same slate every checked button,
toggle group and kit segment uses. That is 3.92:1 or more from the toolbar
and from the off buttons in light and 4.11:1 in dark, with the glyph at
4.90:1 and 5.99:1. On a smoked frost or glass toolbar the header bar
redefines the properties, and the slate stands 4.27:1 or more from the veil.

The rules sit after 0024's, at the same specificity, so they win by order,
and they reach both the view controls and the view-mode controls.
---
diff --git a/src/resources/style.css b/src/resources/style.css
--- a/src/resources/style.css
+++ b/src/resources/style.css
@@ -1308,6 +1308,19 @@
 window.luma-files-window .luma-view-mode-controls button:checked image {
   color: @luma_content;
 }
+
+/* ADR-043: the selected view is a state, not the toolbar's emphasis. It takes
+ * the shared state slate from libadwaita (0039), in every appearance mode. */
+window.luma-files-window .luma-view-controls button:checked,
+window.luma-files-window .luma-view-mode-controls button:checked {
+  background-color: var(--luma-state);
+  color: var(--luma-state-ink);
+}
+
+window.luma-files-window .luma-view-controls button:checked image,
+window.luma-files-window .luma-view-mode-controls button:checked image {
+  color: var(--luma-state-ink);
+}
 
 /* Reviewed against the desktop Filer simulator: compact native list rows,
  * readable metadata and one continuous material per browsing column. */
